IMPORT prelude

-- Supply Act 2026 (Singapore, No. 6 of 2026) -- commencement (s 1), the ceilings on issue from the Consolidated Fund (s 2) and the
-- Development Fund (s 3), and the Schedule of Heads of Expenditure with the sum appropriated to each Head from each Fund.
--
-- Edition: Act 6 of 2026, informal consolidation, "version in force from 1/4/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SA2026.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The deposit annotates no
-- amendment. The deposited .txt scrambles the Schedule's columns (figures drift between rows and columns). The figures below were
-- read from the deposited PDF (SA2026.pdf, same bundle) with pdftotext -table, which keeps each Head's row together; every row then
-- adds across, and every column adds down to the totals in ss 2(1) and 3(1). Those checks are asserted in the case file.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0223 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The answer, on the text, is nothing directly: the Act authorises the Government to issue money and
-- appropriates it to Heads of Expenditure. It confers no right, duty, eligibility, offence or remedy on any private person.
--
-- Not encoded: anything outside the deposit -- the Constitution, the Financial Procedure Act, the
-- Development Fund Act, the Estimates and the subheads beneath each Head, supplementary supply, virement. Whether a Head's sum is a
-- binding cap on issue for that Head is not stated in the Act; the per-Head rule below is labelled an INFERENCE.
--
-- Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers (20260401 is 1 April 2026) so that they compare in order. This is an encoding device.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Supply Act 2026`

§§ `1 -- commencement`

-- s 1: "This Act is the Supply Act 2026 and comes into operation on 1 April 2026."
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is in operation on` IF
    `the date` AT LEAST 20260401

-- ss 2(1), 3(1): each sum is authorised to be issued "for the period starting 1 April 2026 and ending 31 March 2027".
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date falls in the supply period` IF
        `the date` AT LEAST 20260401
    AND `the date` AT MOST 20270331

§§ `2, 3 -- the two Funds and their ceilings`

DECLARE Fund IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Fund`
    `the Development Fund`

-- s 2(1): "A sum of not more than $158,962,520,000 is authorised to be issued from the Consolidated Fund for the period starting
-- 1 April 2026 and ending 31 March 2027." (2): "appropriated for the Heads of Expenditure for the public service specified in the
-- Schedule".
-- s 3(1): "A sum of not more than $49,014,559,600 is authorised to be issued from the Development Fund" for the same period. (2):
-- "appropriated for development purposes under the Heads of Expenditure specified in the Schedule".
GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling on issue from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fund`
    WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN 158962520000
    WHEN `the Development Fund` THEN 49014559600

-- s 2(1) / 3(1): an issue is within the Act's authority if it is made in the supply period and the Fund's issues for the period,
-- this one included, do not pass "not more than" the ceiling.
GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund, `already issued in the period` IS A NUMBER, `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the date of issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issue is within the ceiling` IF
        `the date falls in the supply period` `the date of issue`
    AND `already issued in the period` PLUS `the amount` AT MOST `the ceiling on issue from` `the fund`

§§ `Schedule -- Heads of Expenditure`

-- The Schedule ("Sections 2(2) and 3(2)") lists 23 Heads, lettered B to Z with no A, H or Y. Each has an "Appropriation from
-- Consolidated Fund", an "Appropriation from Development Fund" and a "Total appropriations". Where the Schedule prints "..." for a
-- Fund it is read here as nil (0) -- an inference from the totals, which add up only if "..." is zero.
DECLARE Head IS ONE OF
    `B Attorney-General's Chambers`
    `C Auditor-General's Office`
    `D Cabinet Office`
    `E Judicature`
    `F Parliament`
    `G Presidential Councils`
    `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`
    `J Ministry of Defence`
    `K Ministry of Education`
    `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`
    `M Ministry of Finance`
    `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs`
    `O Ministry of Health`
    `P Ministry of Home Affairs`
    `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    `R Ministry of Law`
    `S Ministry of Manpower`
    `T Ministry of National Development`
    `U Prime Minister's Office`
    `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    `W Ministry of Transport`
    `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth`
    `Z Financial Transfers`

GIVETH A LIST OF Head
`every Head in the Schedule` MEANS
    LIST `B Attorney-General's Chambers`, `C Auditor-General's Office`, `D Cabinet Office`, `E Judicature`, `F Parliament`,
         `G Presidential Councils`, `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`, `J Ministry of Defence`, `K Ministry of Education`,
         `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`, `M Ministry of Finance`, `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs`,
         `O Ministry of Health`, `P Ministry of Home Affairs`, `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`, `R Ministry of Law`,
         `S Ministry of Manpower`, `T Ministry of National Development`, `U Prime Minister's Office`, `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`,
         `W Ministry of Transport`, `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth`, `Z Financial Transfers`

-- Schedule, column "Appropriation from Consolidated Fund $".
GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `B Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN 306697200
    WHEN `C Auditor-General's Office` THEN 48279100
    WHEN `D Cabinet Office` THEN 1200000
    WHEN `E Judicature` THEN 415644700
    WHEN `F Parliament` THEN 50739900
    WHEN `G Presidential Councils` THEN 1724400
    WHEN `I Ministry of Social and Family Development` THEN 5822529800
    WHEN `J Ministry of Defence` THEN 23343497600
    WHEN `K Ministry of Education` THEN 15473381200
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 2890738400
    WHEN `M Ministry of Finance` THEN 1252309600
    WHEN `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs` THEN 614402500
    WHEN `O Ministry of Health` THEN 20035377700
    WHEN `P Ministry of Home Affairs` THEN 9242695600
    WHEN `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information` THEN 2993365900
    WHEN `R Ministry of Law` THEN 417819500
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 3920999400
    WHEN `T Ministry of National Development` THEN 8640058800
    WHEN `U Prime Minister's Office` THEN 716873400
    WHEN `V Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN 1861722800
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 3109174200
    WHEN `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth` THEN 2407711100
    WHEN `Z Financial Transfers` THEN 55395577200

-- Schedule, column "Appropriation from Development Fund $". "..." for D Cabinet Office, G Presidential Councils and Z Financial
-- Transfers, read as nil.
GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Development Fund appropriation for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `B Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN 2242700
    WHEN `C Auditor-General's Office` THEN 876000
    WHEN `D Cabinet Office` THEN 0
    WHEN `E Judicature` THEN 12333800
    WHEN `F Parliament` THEN 12792700
    WHEN `G Presidential Councils` THEN 0
    WHEN `I Ministry of Social and Family Development` THEN 259759300
    WHEN `J Ministry of Defence` THEN 2454719600
    WHEN `K Ministry of Education` THEN 1185000000
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 820076600
    WHEN `M Ministry of Finance` THEN 68615100
    WHEN `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs` THEN 46700000
    WHEN `O Ministry of Health` THEN 2467566400
    WHEN `P Ministry of Home Affairs` THEN 2672087400
    WHEN `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information` THEN 119025200
    WHEN `R Ministry of Law` THEN 287047600
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 178690100
    WHEN `T Ministry of National Development` THEN 13613535500
    WHEN `U Prime Minister's Office` THEN 123553300
    WHEN `V Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN 10705745500
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 13306280300
    WHEN `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth` THEN 677912500
    WHEN `Z Financial Transfers` THEN 0

-- Schedule, column "Total appropriations $", transcribed separately so that the row arithmetic can be checked against it.
GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the printed total for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `B Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN 308939900
    WHEN `C Auditor-General's Office` THEN 49155100
    WHEN `D Cabinet Office` THEN 1200000
    WHEN `E Judicature` THEN 427978500
    WHEN `F Parliament` THEN 63532600
    WHEN `G Presidential Councils` THEN 1724400
    WHEN `I Ministry of Social and Family Development` THEN 6082289100
    WHEN `J Ministry of Defence` THEN 25798217200
    WHEN `K Ministry of Education` THEN 16658381200
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 3710815000
    WHEN `M Ministry of Finance` THEN 1320924700
    WHEN `N Ministry of Foreign Affairs` THEN 661102500
    WHEN `O Ministry of Health` THEN 22502944100
    WHEN `P Ministry of Home Affairs` THEN 11914783000
    WHEN `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information` THEN 3112391100
    WHEN `R Ministry of Law` THEN 704867100
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 4099689500
    WHEN `T Ministry of National Development` THEN 22253594300
    WHEN `U Prime Minister's Office` THEN 840426700
    WHEN `V Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN 12567468300
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 16415454500
    WHEN `X Ministry of Culture, Community and Youth` THEN 3085623600
    WHEN `Z Financial Transfers` THEN 55395577200

-- The Schedule's "Total" row: 158,962,520,000 / 49,014,559,600 / 207,977,079,600.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the printed grand total` MEANS 207977079600

GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund, `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the appropriation from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fund`
    WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `the head`
    WHEN `the Development Fund` THEN `the Development Fund appropriation for` `the head`

GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total appropriation for` MEANS
    `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `the head` PLUS `the Development Fund appropriation for` `the head`

GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row adds up for` IF
    `the total appropriation for` `the head` EQUALS `the printed total for` `the head`

GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Development Fund gives more than the Consolidated Fund to` IF
    `the Development Fund appropriation for` `the head` GREATER THAN `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `the head`

GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund, hs IS A LIST OF Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum appropriated from` MEANS
    CONSIDER hs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the appropriation from` `the fund` h PLUS `the sum appropriated from` `the fund` rest

GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule's column total for` MEANS
    `the sum appropriated from` `the fund` `every Head in the Schedule`

GIVEN hs IS A LIST OF Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of` MEANS
    CONSIDER hs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN 1 PLUS `the number of` rest

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of Heads` MEANS `the number of` `every Head in the Schedule`

GIVEN hs IS A LIST OF Head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `each row adds up among` IF
    CONSIDER hs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the row adds up for` h AND `each row adds up among` rest

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every row adds up` IF
    `each row adds up among` `every Head in the Schedule`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grand total of the Schedule` MEANS
    `the Schedule's column total for` `the Consolidated Fund` PLUS `the Schedule's column total for` `the Development Fund`

-- ss 2(2), 3(2) appropriate each ceiling "for the Heads of Expenditure ... specified in the Schedule". The Schedule's column must then
-- exhaust the ceiling. Checked, not assumed.
GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule column equals the ceiling for` IF
    `the Schedule's column total for` `the fund` EQUALS `the ceiling on issue from` `the fund`

-- INFERENCE. The Act does not say in terms that issue for a Head may not exceed that Head's sum; it says the whole sum "is
-- appropriated for the Heads ... specified in the Schedule" and the Schedule gives a sum per Head. Read as a per-Head cap, a Head with
-- "..." in a Fund's column has nothing appropriated to it from that Fund.
GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund, `the head` IS A Head, `already issued for the head` IS A NUMBER, `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the date of issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issue is within the Head's appropriation` IF
        `the date falls in the supply period` `the date of issue`
    AND `already issued for the head` PLUS `the amount` AT MOST `the appropriation from` `the fund` `the head`

§§ `What the Act decides for a person or business (REQ-0223)`

-- Nothing in ss 1-3 or the Schedule names a private person, confers a right or entitlement, imposes a duty, creates an offence or
-- gives a remedy. Every operative verb is addressed to the Government's Funds ("is authorised to be issued", "is appropriated").
DECLARE Question IS ONE OF
    `does the Act give a person a right to any payment`
    `does the Act impose a duty on a person or business`
    `does the Act create an offence`
    `does the Act authorise sums to be issued from the Funds`
    `does the Act appropriate money to a Ministry's Head`

GIVEN `the question` IS A Question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act answers yes to` IF
    CONSIDER `the question`
    WHEN `does the Act authorise sums to be issued from the Funds` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `does the Act appropriate money to a Ministry's Head` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
